        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Catfish and the Bottlemen, The Lumineers\n- Albums: The Balcony\n- Songs: \"Stubborn Love\"\n- Places: Llandudno, Wales; Denver, Colorado; Ramsey, New Jersey\n- Genres: Rock, Folk rock, Americana\n\nFacts:\n- The Lumineers' members Schultz and Fraites began writing and performing together in Ramsey, New Jersey in 2005.\n- Catfish and the Bottlemen are a British rock band that formed in Llandudno, Wales in 2007.\n- In the 2010s, The Lumineers became one of the most popular folk rock and Americana artists during the revival of those genres.\n- The Lumineers are an American folk rock and Americana band based in Denver, Colorado.\n- The Balcony is the debut studio album by Welsh rock band Catfish and the Bottlemen.\n- \"Stubborn Love\" is a song by American folk rock band The Lumineers.",
